I now have a thorough picture. Note: the grep for `@RestController`/`@PostMapping` returned nothing — this project has no traditional Spring MVC controllers; the "Spring arm" is the MapStruct/JPA/repository layer, and the request flow is driven entirely by OfficeFloor YAML wiring plus function classes.

## 1. `registrationDate` — where set / defaulted / validated

**Field definition** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:54-55`
```java
@Column(name = "registration_date", columnDefinition = "DATE")
private LocalDate registrationDate;
```
Getter/setter at lines 101-107.

**Default-to-server-date** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java:19-21`
```java
if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
    owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
}
```
This is the FIRST step of the create flow (`build:` in the YAML). It defaults to `LocalDate.now()` with NO business-day / weekend / holiday adjustment.

**DB schema** — column `registration_date DATE` in all four dialects:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/db/h2/schema.sql:39`
- `.../db/hsqldb/schema.sql`, `.../db/postgres/schema.sql`, `.../db/mysql/schema.sql`

**API contract** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml:2042-2047`: "The date the pet owner was registered; defaults to the server's current date when omitted." (`format: date`).

No explicit validator class for `registrationDate` (it's optional in the request DTO).

## 2. Owner creation flow (POST /owners)

There is NO Spring `@RestController`. The endpoint is defined purely by OfficeFloor YAML:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** — authorize `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, then a linear chain (each `next:` links to the following):
1. `build` → `BuildOwner` (maps DTO→Owner, defaults registrationDate)
2. `normalizeTelephone` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`
3. `normalizeAddress` → `NormalizeOwnerAddress`
4. `ensureUniqueTelephone` → `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone`
5. `ensureUniqueHousehold` → `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`
6. `ensureCityCapacity` → `EnsureCityHasCapacity`
7. `ensureDailyCapacity` → `EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity`
8. `assignCustomerCode` → `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`
9. `countNamesakes` → `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`
10. `save` → `SaveOwner`
11. `respond` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`

All function classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`.

**Signature of the entry function** — `BuildOwner.service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> requestOut)`.

The DTO→entity mapping is `OwnerMapper.toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java:48`.

## 3. Membership number generation (year segment from registration date)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java:36-42`** (computed on READ, in `toOwnerDto`):
```java
/** '<customerCode>-M<YY>', YY = last two digits of the registrationDate year; null when either input is absent. */
default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
}
```
Wired via `@Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", expression = "java(membershipNumber(owner))")` at line 25. The "year segment" is `-M<YY>` where `YY = registrationDate.getYear() % 100`.

The `customerCode` prefix it builds on is assigned at create time by **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`): format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city 4-digit sequence, e.g. `LON-SMI-0007`). Note this customerCode itself does NOT use the year — the year segment is added only in `membershipNumber`.

Related derived field: `membershipTier` (`OwnerMapper.java:31-34`) — SILVER when `namesakeCount==0` and email present, else BRONZE. Openapi docs at `openapi.yml:2101-2108`.

## 4. Daily create-limit (owners per day)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity.java`**
```java
private static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;

public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DailyRegistrationLimitException {
    LocalDate today = owner.getRegistrationDate();
    long count = 0;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (!Objects.equals(existing.getId(), owner.getId())
                && today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate())) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    if (count >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
        throw new DailyRegistrationLimitException("The maximum number of owners for today has been reached");
    }
}
```
Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's `registrationDate` (its default is today); rejects at ≥100.

- Exception: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyRegistrationLimitException.java`
- Handler → HTTP 429: `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../escalation/DailyRegistrationLimitExceptionHandler.java` (maps to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`).

Parallel per-city cap (50) is `EnsureCityHasCapacity.java` / `CityAtCapacityException` (429-ish handler), for comparison.

## 5. Existing tests

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — one test, `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay()`:
```java
int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
```
It asserts the default registrationDate is never a weekend (a "business-day roll" rule). Important discrepancy worth flagging: the current `BuildOwner` sets a plain `LocalDate.now()` with no weekend/holiday roll, so this test would fail on weekends/holidays. The rolling helper exists only in the test base, not in production code.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — the harness (hits `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}` via MockMvc). Relevant helpers:
- `today()` (line 110-112) → `LocalDate.now().toString()`.
- `createMany(int n)` (line 183-187) — "Create n owners all dated today — used to drive the per-day create-limit / bulk-signup rules." Directly targets the daily create-limit.
- `fillCity(String city, int n)` (line 173-179) — drives the per-city capacity rule.
- `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (line 268-274) — rolls over Saturdays, Sundays, and `HOLIDAYS`.
- `HOLIDAYS` set (line 240-242) for 2026.
